WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.644
You are awake.

00:00:01.594 --> 00:00:08.623
It is somewhere around three in the morning, and it happened again after a stretch of nights where it did not.

00:00:08.623 --> 00:00:11.755
Before anything else, one fact.

00:00:11.755 --> 00:00:14.197
Nothing you built has been undone.

00:00:14.197 --> 00:00:22.785
One night awake does not remove the sleep drive you rebuilt, it does not move your anchor, and it does not put you back where you started.

00:00:22.785 --> 00:00:28.873
What puts you back is what you do in the next twenty minutes, and in the twelve hours after you get up.

00:00:28.873 --> 00:00:31.373
That is what this recording is for.

00:00:31.373 --> 00:00:35.211
Twenty minutes, in the dark, with your eyes closed.

00:00:35.211 --> 00:00:37.961
You do not have to hold anything in your head.

00:00:37.961 --> 00:00:40.741
I will tell you when to act and when to wait.

00:00:40.741 --> 00:00:42.520
Set the volume low.

00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:46.976
Once this is playing, put the phone face down and out of reach.

00:00:46.976 --> 00:00:49.770
And do not look at the clock again tonight.

00:00:49.770 --> 00:00:53.594
Whatever time it is, the instruction is the same.

00:01:03.772 --> 00:01:06.816
Here is what is happening in your body right now.

00:01:06.766 --> 00:01:12.927
Cortisol starts climbing a few hours before your wake time, because it is what gets you up.

00:01:12.927 --> 00:01:18.883
Most of the night's sleep pressure has already been spent, since you have been asleep for hours.

00:01:18.883 --> 00:01:23.486
So around three, you are cheap to wake and expensive to settle.

00:01:23.486 --> 00:01:28.736
A noise, a full bladder, half a thought, any of it is enough.

00:01:28.736 --> 00:01:32.457
That part is normal, and good sleepers do it too.

00:01:32.457 --> 00:01:39.751
They wake, they do not check the time, they do not ask what it means, and they are gone again in ninety seconds.

00:01:39.751 --> 00:01:42.354
So the difference is not the waking.

00:01:42.354 --> 00:01:45.369
The difference is the alarm that follows it.

00:01:45.369 --> 00:02:00.869
The moment you notice you are awake and start calculating, how many hours are left, whether tomorrow is ruined, whether the method has stopped working, your body reads all of that as a reason to be alert, and it obliges.

00:02:00.869 --> 00:02:04.633
And a relapse after a good stretch is expected.

00:02:04.633 --> 00:02:08.016
It is written into the protocol you already own.

00:02:08.016 --> 00:02:12.810
A bad night after a good week is not evidence that this does not work for you.

00:02:12.810 --> 00:02:15.163
It is the ordinary shape of it.

00:02:23.356 --> 00:02:25.885
So the rule for tonight is this.

00:02:25.835 --> 00:02:27.908
You are not trying to sleep.

00:02:27.908 --> 00:02:34.791
Trying is the pressure that keeps you awake, and it is the one thing guaranteed to make the next hour worse.

00:02:34.791 --> 00:02:38.585
Tonight has two jobs, and neither of them is sleep.

00:02:38.585 --> 00:02:45.570
The first is to keep your bed a place where your body expects to rest, not a place where it expects to fight.

00:02:45.570 --> 00:02:51.776
The second is to protect tomorrow's wake time, because that is what buys back the next night.

00:02:51.776 --> 00:02:53.570
If you sleep, good.

00:02:53.570 --> 00:02:58.908
If you do not, you will still have done both jobs, and the night still counts.

00:02:58.908 --> 00:03:02.070
Let that be true for the next twenty minutes.

00:03:10.252 --> 00:03:14.502
We start with your body, because it is faster than your thoughts.

00:03:14.452 --> 00:03:16.128
Stay where you are.

00:03:16.128 --> 00:03:17.554
Do not move yet.

00:03:17.554 --> 00:03:19.422
Let your jaw come apart.

00:03:19.422 --> 00:03:22.187
Most people wake with the teeth touching.

00:03:22.187 --> 00:03:30.334
Let the lower jaw hang until the teeth are no longer in contact, and let your tongue rest away from the roof of your mouth.

00:03:42.484 --> 00:03:45.675
Let your shoulders drop away from your ears.

00:03:45.625 --> 00:03:50.551
Let your hands open, palms loose, fingers uncurled.

00:04:02.716 --> 00:04:04.392
Now the breath.

00:04:04.342 --> 00:04:06.166
Not deep breathing.

00:04:06.166 --> 00:04:10.592
A slow out breath, which is the half that lowers arousal.

00:04:10.592 --> 00:04:12.695
In through your nose for four.

00:04:12.695 --> 00:04:14.298
Hold for seven.

00:04:14.298 --> 00:04:19.636
Out through your mouth for eight, slowly, the way you would fog a window.

00:04:19.636 --> 00:04:20.724
Begin.

00:04:39.892 --> 00:04:41.127
Again.

00:05:00.724 --> 00:05:01.959
Again.

00:05:21.076 --> 00:05:22.826
Keep going on your own.

00:05:22.776 --> 00:05:25.687
Four in, seven held, eight out.

00:06:25.852 --> 00:06:29.278
Let the breath go back to whatever it wants to do.

00:06:37.396 --> 00:06:40.866
Now check one thing, and check it honestly.

00:06:40.816 --> 00:06:42.860
Not whether you are asleep.

00:06:42.860 --> 00:06:45.934
Whether your body feels heavy or wired.

00:06:45.934 --> 00:06:47.846
Heavy is a good sign.

00:06:47.846 --> 00:06:54.581
Eyes want to stay closed, limbs feel far away, the thoughts have gone loose and strange.

00:06:54.581 --> 00:06:57.316
If that is you, stay where you are.

00:06:57.316 --> 00:07:00.066
Stop this recording if that is easier.

00:07:00.066 --> 00:07:03.610
Let the rest of the night happen without supervision.

00:07:03.610 --> 00:07:05.419
Wired is different.

00:07:05.419 --> 00:07:13.007
Chest fast, mind in full sentences, legs restless, the feeling of lying at attention.

00:07:13.007 --> 00:07:14.890
If that is you, get up.

00:07:14.890 --> 00:07:19.184
That is not a punishment and it is not giving up on the night.

00:07:19.184 --> 00:07:23.963
It is the one move that keeps your bed from becoming the place where you lie awake.

00:07:23.963 --> 00:07:30.831
Stay in bed wired for an hour tonight, then again next month, and the bed itself starts to wake you.

00:07:30.831 --> 00:07:35.154
That costs far more than the sleep you lose by leaving it now.

00:07:35.154 --> 00:07:37.243
So: heavy, stay.

00:07:37.243 --> 00:07:38.963
Wired, get up.

00:07:38.963 --> 00:07:44.816
Take the phone only because this recording is on it, and keep it face down and dark.

00:07:59.980 --> 00:08:04.685
If you are up, keep the lights as low as you can still see by.

00:08:04.635 --> 00:08:11.400
No overhead light, no mirror light in the bathroom, no screen at full brightness.

00:08:11.400 --> 00:08:20.032
Bright light at this hour is a wake signal your body clock takes seriously, and it can cost you tomorrow night as well as this one.

00:08:20.032 --> 00:08:23.974
Go somewhere that is not the bedroom and sit in a chair.

00:08:23.974 --> 00:08:25.974
Not lying on the sofa.

00:08:25.974 --> 00:08:27.224
A chair.

00:08:27.224 --> 00:08:33.165
Put something over your shoulders, because you will get cold, and cold will keep you up.

00:08:33.165 --> 00:08:36.356
Now the writing, if there is anything running.

00:08:36.356 --> 00:08:38.400
Paper, not phone.

00:08:38.400 --> 00:08:42.077
You are not solving it and you are not making a good list.

00:08:42.077 --> 00:08:49.282
You are moving what is circling out of your head and onto a surface, so your brain stops rehearsing it to keep it available.

00:08:49.282 --> 00:08:51.782
Write until the loop goes quiet.

00:08:51.782 --> 00:08:53.194
I will wait.

00:11:23.356 --> 00:11:25.767
If more is coming, add it.

00:11:25.717 --> 00:11:29.056
If nothing is coming, put the pen down.

00:11:29.056 --> 00:11:31.232
At the bottom write one line.

00:11:31.232 --> 00:11:37.835
The first thing I will do about this is, and then the smallest next action, tomorrow, in daylight.

00:11:37.835 --> 00:11:41.629
That is the line that closes the file until morning.

00:12:11.788 --> 00:12:17.067
If there was nothing to write, or you are done writing, read something boring.

00:12:17.017 --> 00:12:24.032
Something you have read before, a manual, a magazine you do not care about, on paper if you have it.

00:12:24.032 --> 00:12:28.693
Not news, not messages, not fiction that pulls you along.

00:12:28.693 --> 00:12:31.296
You are not forcing sleepiness.

00:12:31.296 --> 00:12:34.958
You are giving your attention somewhere flat to land.

00:12:45.124 --> 00:12:49.991
And if you stayed in bed because you were heavy, this next part is for you.

00:12:49.941 --> 00:12:53.529
If you are in the chair, keep it for when you go back.

00:12:53.529 --> 00:12:57.647
At three in the morning the mind wants to think in straight lines.

00:12:57.647 --> 00:13:01.206
What happened, what it means, what to do about it.

00:13:01.206 --> 00:13:04.088
Sleep does not start in straight lines.

00:13:04.088 --> 00:13:10.750
It starts when thinking goes scattered and picture based, and that is a state you can imitate on purpose.

00:13:10.750 --> 00:13:12.529
So pick a word.

00:13:12.529 --> 00:13:16.235
Any ordinary word, five or six letters.

00:13:16.235 --> 00:13:26.265
Take its first letter and think of unrelated objects that start with that letter, one at a time, seeing each one for a second before the next.

00:13:26.265 --> 00:13:30.059
Not a list, not a category, not in order.

00:13:30.059 --> 00:13:34.941
If a real problem shows up, notice it and go back to the letter.

00:13:34.941 --> 00:13:40.691
When the letter runs dry, move on to the next letter of your word and carry on.

00:13:40.691 --> 00:13:42.882
That is the whole technique.

00:13:42.882 --> 00:13:44.265
Start now.

00:13:44.265 --> 00:13:45.926
I will be quiet.

00:17:16.132 --> 00:17:19.705
If you are in the chair, here is when you go back to bed.

00:17:19.655 --> 00:17:24.243
When your eyes are closing on their own and you are reading the same line twice.

00:17:24.243 --> 00:17:27.140
Not when you feel you have waited long enough.

00:17:27.140 --> 00:17:32.626
Sleepy and tired are not the same thing, and only sleepy travels.

00:17:32.626 --> 00:17:39.067
When you go back, lights stay off, no clock, no assessment of how the night is going.

00:17:39.067 --> 00:17:46.023
If you are wired again after twenty minutes or so, get up again and run this the same way.

00:17:46.023 --> 00:17:49.537
For most people it takes one or two rounds.

00:17:49.537 --> 00:17:53.273
Doing it twice tonight is not a failure of the method.

00:17:53.273 --> 00:17:54.787
It is the method.

00:18:04.972 --> 00:18:12.766
The last part matters more than everything before it, so if you are still awake, stay with me for two minutes.

00:18:12.716 --> 00:18:17.054
Tomorrow morning is where tonight either ends or repeats.

00:18:17.054 --> 00:18:19.216
Get up at your normal wake time.

00:18:19.216 --> 00:18:20.627
The same one.

00:18:20.627 --> 00:18:27.304
Not thirty minutes later to make up for this, not two hours later because it is the weekend.

00:18:27.304 --> 00:18:33.495
One late morning re-opens the whole thing, because it spends the pressure you need for tomorrow night.

00:18:33.495 --> 00:18:37.730
Get light into your eyes in the first half hour of being up.

00:18:37.730 --> 00:18:42.319
Outside if you can, ten minutes, even under cloud.

00:18:42.319 --> 00:18:43.716
Do not nap.

00:18:43.716 --> 00:18:50.745
If you truly cannot function, twenty minutes, before three in the afternoon, and no longer.

00:18:50.745 --> 00:18:54.921
Caffeine as usual in the morning, none after midday.

00:18:54.921 --> 00:19:00.495
You are going to want more today, and more today is how tomorrow night goes the same way.

00:19:00.495 --> 00:19:04.054
And do not go to bed early tonight to catch up.

00:19:04.054 --> 00:19:07.274
Same bedtime, or slightly later.

00:19:07.274 --> 00:19:15.642
That is the part almost everyone gets wrong, and it is the fastest way to turn one bad night into a bad week.

00:19:25.828 --> 00:19:27.828
That is the protocol.

00:19:27.778 --> 00:19:31.101
Tomorrow, one line in your sleep log.

00:19:31.101 --> 00:19:33.645
What woke you and what you did.

00:19:33.645 --> 00:19:35.645
Not a score for the night.

00:19:35.645 --> 00:19:40.704
If this repeats three nights in a row, that is still not an emergency.

00:19:40.704 --> 00:19:44.851
Run Night 4 and Night 5 again and give it a week.

00:19:44.851 --> 00:19:48.513
One thing said once, and then I will leave you alone.

00:19:48.513 --> 00:19:52.483
This is education and coaching, not medical care.

00:19:52.483 --> 00:20:06.145
If the waking comes with pain, with trouble breathing, or with a heart that will not settle, or if your mood has been low for weeks, that is a conversation with a doctor, not a protocol.

00:20:06.145 --> 00:20:08.836
And here is the part worth keeping.

00:20:08.836 --> 00:20:13.248
The fear that it comes back is not proof that it is coming back.

00:20:13.248 --> 00:20:16.822
Tonight it came back and you had something to do about it.

00:20:16.822 --> 00:20:20.645
That is already a different night from the ones you used to have.

00:20:20.645 --> 00:20:22.307
Close your eyes.

00:20:22.307 --> 00:20:25.380
Nothing else is required of you until morning.
